                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ee4baa4-14eb-35c1-b9c0-aa53a4dd5743",
                        "entry_id": "5c918073-a584-365e-b3fe-b867a902cca5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who believes in a first cause."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6fc5316-bbf3-434a-873f-a8e8c9be847f",
                                "sense_id": "1ee4baa4-14eb-35c1-b9c0-aa53a4dd5743",
                                "text": "That which is \"morally good (correct, right)\" will have the same meaning, in most cases, for the Causationist ( or Determinist ) as it does for the Libertarian or Compatibilist ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ecaa5c3-6c25-4e72-a8d4-25354458a3a8",
                                "sense_id": "1ee4baa4-14eb-35c1-b9c0-aa53a4dd5743",
                                "text": "As a \"causationist,\" Emerson believes that there is \"not a weak or cracked link in the chain that joins the first and last of things,\" and he defines \"causality,\" therefore, as \"strict connexion between every pulse-beat and the principle of being\" (\"Power,\", CW 6:29)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
